// DYNAMIC.md §6.5: a `#[test]` fn lowers normally AND registers itself on the
// module-level `__tests` table the runtime walks (§7) — `__tests["name"] = name`.
// No prior case exercised it; no backend emitted the registration. Two `#[test]`
// fns pin that `__tests` is declared once and accrues one entry per test, keyed
// by name; `main`, an ordinary `fn`, gets no entry — registration is gated on the
// attribute. main calls both tests so the run trial observes their bodies execute
// after the registration statements run at load; the emit golden pins the
// `__tests` table and its entries. The Rust anchor omits `#[test]` (it has no
// runtime-observable effect in a plain binary) and mirrors only the stdout, as
// the derive cases do.
extern {
    fn println(s: string);
}

#[test]
fn checks_alpha() {
    println("alpha-ran");
}

#[test]
fn checks_beta() {
    println("beta-ran");
}

fn main() {
    checks_alpha();
    checks_beta();
}
